.TH TTYCHATTER.MAILBOT 1 "May 2026" "ttychatter.mailbot 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ttychatter.mailbot \- email transport adapter and remote control surface for ttychatter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--config-file PATH] [--once|--daemon] [--dry-run] [--open-to-public]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--doctor] [--list-candidates] [--cleanup-public-sessions]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--config|--raw-config] [--sessions|--list-sessions] [--manpage]
[--model-cache] [--model-search TEXT] [--update-models]
[--delete-session SESSION]
.PP
.B ttychatter.mailbot
[--set KEY VALUE] [--unset KEY] [--set-imap-password [--gpg]]
[--set-smtp-password [--gpg]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ttychatter.mailbot reads unread IMAP mail, maps each accepted message to a
chat session or an allowlisted control command, calls ttychatter.python when
chat or ttychatter utility work is needed, and replies by sendmail or SMTP.
.PP
Private mode requires ALLOWED_FROM. Public demo mode, enabled by
.B --open-to-public
or OPEN_TO_PUBLIC=1, accepts mail from any sender but restricts non-ALLOWED_FROM
senders to public chat and the PUBLIC_ALLOWED_COMMANDS set.
.SH PRIVATE SUBJECT GRAMMAR
.TP
.B tc:{session-name}
Send the message body to the named ttychatter session.
.TP
.B tc:{new}
Start a new unnamed chat. The mailbot passes no session argument, so
ttychatter.python creates its normal timestamped session name.
.TP
.B tc:CONFIG
Export or apply the mailbot config attachment.
.TP
.B tc:MODELS
Return the existing MODEL_CACHE_FILE as models-cache.json. This is cache-only;
it does not call ttychatter.python --update-models.
.TP
.B tc:MODELS TEXT
Search the existing model cache for TEXT. This is also cache-only.
.TP
.B tc:CMD
Run the first nonempty message-body line as a mailbot command.
.TP
.B tc:command args
Run a mailbot command directly from the subject.
.TP
.B MAILBOT
When included in BODY_COMMAND_SUBJECTS, use the first nonempty body line as
the command or session selector. "session NAME" and "chat NAME" route the
remaining body to that chat session.
.SH PUBLIC DEMO MODE
In public mode, a message without a recognized control subject is treated as
an AI prompt. PUBLIC_SESSION_MODE controls isolation: per-sender, per-message,
or shared. The default is per-sender. Replies to public users use
"Re: public-session-name" so the user can resume by replying with that subject.
.PP
Public sessions use PUBLIC_SESSION_PREFIX and are cleaned up automatically
when PUBLIC_SESSION_CLEANUP=1. PUBLIC_SESSION_IDLE_HOURS,
PUBLIC_SESSION_TTL_HOURS, and PUBLIC_SESSION_MAX_COUNT control deletion.
PUBLIC_SESSION_MAX_TURNS trims surviving public logs to the most recent
input/output cycles. Cleanup matches PUBLIC_SESSION_PREFIX-*.log logs and
the configured shared public log when PUBLIC_SESSION_MODE=shared.
.PP
When PUBLIC_SESSION_ARCHIVE_ON_DELETE=1, an expiring public log is emailed
to the recorded sender before local deletion. PUBLIC_SESSION_ARCHIVE_USER_TOGGLE=1
lets public users change their own preference with archive-session on/off.
PUBLIC_SESSION_ARCHIVE_FAILURE_POLICY=keep refuses deletion when archive
sending fails; delete removes the local log anyway.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Return the email command summary.
.TP
.B manpage
Return this roff manpage. Aliases: manual, get-manpage, fetch-manpage.
.TP
.B sessions
List saved session names with short head and tail previews.
.TP
.B search TEXT
Search all session logs for TEXT.
.TP
.B search-session SESSION TEXT
Search one session log.
.TP
.B rename-session OLD NEW
Rename a session log.
.TP
.B delete-session SESSION
Delete a session log. Aliases: delete, rm, remove-session, rm-session.
The target must resolve inside SESSION_DIR and the supplied name must already
be the exact sanitized session name. Use --dry-run locally to show the path
that would be deleted without deleting it.
.TP
.B archive-session [on|off|status]
Show or change the sender's public-mode archive-on-expire preference. Aliases:
archive-opt-in and archive-opt-out.
.TP
.B model-cache
Return the existing MODEL_CACHE_FILE only. Never refreshes the cache.
.TP
.B model-search TEXT
Search the existing model cache only. Never refreshes the cache.
.TP
.B update-models
Explicitly run ttychatter.python --update-models, then return models-cache.json.
.TP
.B model-list [FLAGS]
Run ttychatter.python --models. Aliases include models and list-models.
.TP
.B routers [FLAGS]
Run ttychatter.python --routers.
.SH OUTPUT MODES
COMMAND_OUTPUT_MODE, MODEL_CACHE_OUTPUT, MODEL_SEARCH_OUTPUT,
MODEL_LIST_OUTPUT, SESSIONS_OUTPUT, and CONFIG_OUTPUT accept auto, body, or
attachment. The default is auto globally, with short search/session results
in the body and large cache/config results as attachments.
.SH CONFIGURATION KEYS
Important keys include IMAP_HOST, IMAP_PORT, IMAP_SSL, IMAP_USER,
IMAP_PASSWORD, IMAP_PASSWORD_GPG_FILE, SEND_METHOD, SENDMAIL_PATH,
MAIL_FROM, MAIL_TO, ALLOWED_FROM, SUBJECT_PREFIX, SUBJECT_SEPARATOR,
SESSION_OPEN_DELIM, SESSION_CLOSE_DELIM, BODY_COMMAND_SUBJECTS,
ALLOW_COMMANDS_IN_SUBJECT, ALLOW_BODY_COMMAND_SUBJECTS,
ALLOW_BARE_CONTROL_SUBJECTS, ALLOW_LEGACY_BRACED_CONTROL,
RE_SESSION_SUBJECTS, OPEN_TO_PUBLIC, PUBLIC_SESSION_MODE,
PUBLIC_SESSION_PREFIX, PUBLIC_SHARED_SESSION, PUBLIC_ALLOW_NAMED_SESSIONS,
PUBLIC_ALLOWED_COMMANDS, PUBLIC_SESSION_CLEANUP, PUBLIC_SESSION_TTL_HOURS,
PUBLIC_SESSION_IDLE_HOURS, PUBLIC_SESSION_MAX_COUNT,
PUBLIC_SESSION_MAX_TURNS, PUBLIC_SESSION_INDEX_FILE,
PUBLIC_SESSION_ARCHIVE_ON_DELETE, PUBLIC_SESSION_ARCHIVE_USER_TOGGLE,
PUBLIC_SESSION_ARCHIVE_FAILURE_POLICY, PUBLIC_SESSION_ARCHIVE_MAX_BYTES,
MODEL_CACHE_FILE,
SESSION_DIR, ATTACHMENT_DIR, WORK_DIR, PROCESSED_DB, COMMAND_OUTPUT_MODE,
MODEL_CACHE_OUTPUT, MODEL_SEARCH_OUTPUT, MODEL_LIST_OUTPUT, SESSIONS_OUTPUT,
CONFIG_OUTPUT, OUTPUT_INLINE_MAX_BYTES, MAX_COMMAND_OUTPUT_BYTES, and
MAX_OUTGOING_ATTACHMENT_BYTES.
.SH SECURITY
Public mode is for demos. It should use a separate mailbox, conservative
attachment/body limits, per-sender sessions, and a small PUBLIC_ALLOWED_COMMANDS
set. Do not expose config mutation, model refresh, session deletion, or tty-set
to non-ALLOWED_FROM senders.
.SH FILES
Default config: ~/.config/ttychatter/mailbot/config
.PP
Default processed-message database: ~/.local/state/ttychatter/mailbot/processed-ids.txt
.PP
Default session directory: ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions
.PP
Default model cache: ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/models-cache.json
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 indicates success. Nonzero status indicates configuration, IMAP, SMTP,
sendmail, or ttychatter subprocess failure.
